; ============================================================
;  WHAT THE QUICK KEYS GOVERN
;
;  Squared Away's gate asks one question - is this thing in the rig? -
;  and it only ever asks it about MEDICINE, because kinds = i_medical
;  was the whole of the family. So a cigarette, a flask and a tin of
;  stew were quick from anywhere at all, including the bottom of a
;  backpack, while a bandage in the same backpack was refused.
;
;  This adds the other three consumable kinds, so the rule is one rule:
;  IF YOU WANT IT FAST, IT GOES ON THE RIG.
;
;  WHICH POCKET still decides the rest. With 60 SA Pocket Tags a green
;  square is quick for food, drink, devices and bandages, a red one for
;  those and all medicine, and a yellow one for nothing. That is what
;  the green squares on the rig ladder are FOR, and until this file
;  existed they did not really do anything - food was already fast
;  from everywhere.
;
;  THIS IS THE HARSHEST LINE IN THE SET. Eating out of your rucksack
;  stops working: every meal wants a green square first. If that is a
;  step too far, delete i_food and i_drink from `kinds` below and keep
;  the devices - or disable this mod and nothing else changes.
;
;  ! IS THE OVERRIDE MARKER. This is Squared Away's section; a second
;  plain declaration of it would be fatal at startup.
; ============================================================

![amp_box_medpocket]
kinds = i_medical, i_food, i_drink, i_device
no    = That goes in a pocket you can reach
